  "spec": "The realm as a grid of districts (sim/map/districts.ts). The home district (homeCol, homeRow) holds the hand-made world as generated today; every other district is generated from the seed when something needs it. districtTiles = side of one district in tiles (the grid is cols x rows of them, centred so the home district is centred on the origin). settlements = how many towns and villages a district holds; kinds weights pick each one's size (the first, the district seat, is at least a town). Each district takes a character from the game's own ideas: a wound the place carries (despair range), where it sits between village and city (gapAxis), a doctrine that rules it, a land, and a naming culture.",
